From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: align SGMII link modes with SDK

Keep SGMII, 1000BASE-X, and 2500BASE-X programming in a dedicated
resolved-speed helper.  Configure Clause 37 advertisement and restart
semantics consistently with the Airoha SDK, and check the phylink link
timer error path.  Forced modes now use the resolved speed from link_up,
while in-band 1000BASE-X keeps its fixed 1G PCS rate and restarts
negotiation when its advertisement changes.

This patch is split from the per-port PCS state and USXGMII changes so
that the mode programming and negotiation behavior can be reviewed
independently.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Index: linux-6.18.44/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
===================================================================
